# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The process boundary as a deployment property: the demo panel runs as
# its OWN binary, appears through the window session, publishes its menus
# as the same plain data a linked-in window would -- and the global bar
# cannot tell the difference.
wait 40
expect-title Descriptor Demo
note the frame's pixels came over the wire: the centre of the wordmark's
note 96x3 amber rule, which crossed the process boundary as part of the
note frame rather than being painted by anything in this shell
expect-pixel 365 294 ffcb00
note a drag crosses the process boundary and leaves footprints: MOVE
note paints amber, RELEASE stamps ink -- each round-tripping the wire
press 400 300
move 430 310
move 450 315
wait 4
release 470 320
wait 30
expect-pixel 450 315 ffcb00
expect-pixel 470 320 000000
note its menus reach the strip over the wire
write /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings GlobalMenuBar on
wait 20
click-window Descriptor Demo
wait 4
click 68 8
wait 4
expect-menu Refresh
note and a pick rides the wire back: Quit ends the process, and the
note compositor sweeps the window whose session died
menu-pick Quit
wait 30
expect-no-title Descriptor Demo
quit
